'enclosed' = fraction of directions out of the ligand that run into peptide: is it in a
shell or against one face. 'wrapped' = fraction of ligand atoms with peptide within 4.5 A.
They disagree usefully -- a fold can contact three quarters of the ligand while leaving it
outside, which the centroid separation shows.

